  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cosmicstack-labs/mercury-agent/zipball/v1.2.7",
  "body": "The release where **one key reaches 350+ models.** AI/ML API joins Mercury as a first-class provider, alongside two quiet reliability fixes from the community.\n\n## Highlights\n\n### AI/ML API provider — 350+ chat models on one key\n- New named provider (`AIMLAPI_API_KEY`) with the full setup flow: `mercury setup` validates your key by fetching its live chat catalogue and offers a model pick (recommendation: `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6`)\n- Model discovery is surface-aware: AI/ML API lists chat, image, video and speech models as separate rows with repeated ids — Mercury keeps only the chat surface and collapses the repeats, so the picker shows real chat models instead of \"could not find any supported chat models\"\n- Also configurable through the web UI (Providers page) and `.env` (`AIMLAPI_BASE_URL` / `AIMLAPI_MODEL` / `AIMLAPI_ENABLED`)\n- Without a key it stays unconfigured and unregistered — nothing changes for existing installs; the default provider is untouched\n\n## Fixed\n- **`mercury uninstall` local-install detection** — the project-level npm install was never discoverable (one `dirname()` too many stripped the project directory); the scan now also works on machines with no global install, verified against simulated nvm-managed roots\n- **The bundled ink fixes are now self-sufficient** — previously the log-update diff-render and the live-region guard came only from patch-package, which fails on Termux (Android). The applier now carries the full set (Yoga WASM hygiene, Static identity dedup, freeze gate, live-region guard, diff-render) with a regression test driving a stock ink 5.2.1 tree through it\n\n**Full changelog:** https://github.com/cosmicstack-labs/mercury-agent/compare/v1.2.6...v1.2.7"
}
